proximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=-6)$ can be approximated as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39bb09ec-48b5-5f33-adde-628ba380f524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423902 #edb/ref 1074 "We construct an interval around $X=-6$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](images/9f/9f21d7fe3ba1f4efa7b4e24e3d096d84825ff3712f5854c76dabccf0477f503c.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-6) & ≈P(-6-0.5\\le Y\\le -6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-6.5\\le Y\\le -5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423904 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423904 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423904 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423904 #edb/ref 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(4\\le X\\le 11)$ can be approximated as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423904 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acbfdb28-97bf-5853-92f1-7b02234a722c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423904 #edb/ref 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we extend the endpoints of the interval $4\\le X\\le 11$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4\\le X\\le 11) & ≈P(4-0.5\\le Y\\le 11+0.5) \\\\  & =P(3.5\\le Y\\le 11.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425063 #edb/ref 1080 "P(0.5\\le Y\\le 4.5)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425063 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425063 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01d60f05-c149-5def-b6ca-6ac37c02ecce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425064 #edb/ref 1080 "P(Y\\ge 9.5)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425064 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425064 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07428db6-e061-5594-af12-24a5080b1157" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425065 #edb/ref 1080 "P(1.5\\l