186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425085 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8a65ee43-9417-5b75-9427-c7a5605ab37b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425086 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425086 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425086 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425086 #edb/ref 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=5)$ can be approximated as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425086 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a72d914-d1dc-54af-a5be-bb57f769ce56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425086 #edb/ref 1074 "We construct an interval around $X=5$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](images/b8/b87c1f5bb39d9bd7fe5a46695eb8428909fc40c0e489fd12b054bbd77be8127f.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & ≈P(5-0.5\\le Y\\le 5+0.5) \\\\  & =P(4.5\\le Y\\le 5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425087 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425087 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425087 #edb/ref 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X<17)$ can be approximated as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425087 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72c5955a-7dbc-59eb-bd3a-0c79c37d7f53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425087 #edb/ref 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X<17)=P(X\\le 16)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\le 16$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 16) & ≈P(Y\\le 16+0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 16.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425088 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425088 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425088 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425088 #edb/ref 1071 "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>8)$ can be approximated as" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425088 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "baf96d37-475c-5239-92e4-1c5876314e32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425088 #edb/ref 1074 "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>8)=P(X\\ge 9)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\ge 9$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 9) & ≈P(Y\\ge 9-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 8.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
